## Forms and validation

- **Backend:** All form submissions validated via Form Request classes; no inline validation in controllers (stack-conventions).
- **Frontend:** Use Inertia `useForm()`; with shadcn components (Select, Checkbox) bind via `form.set()` / `onValueChange` (developing-gotchas → Form State with shadcn Components).

---

## Errors and user feedback (fallback / QA)

- **Business-rule failures (e.g. “can’t do X when status is Y”):** Prefer **redirect back with a clear flash message** over returning 403 Unauthorized. Check the condition in the controller (or after authorize), return `redirect()->route(...)->with('error', 'Clear message.')` so the user sees why the action was disallowed instead of a generic “Unauthorized” page.
- **Form Request vs controller:** If the failure is a business rule (e.g. “session is completed”), handle it in the controller so you can redirect with flash. Use the Form Request only for role/permission (so real unauthorized users still get 403).
- **Show flash.error on pages:** On detail/show pages that can receive these redirects, display `flash.error` the same way as `flash.success`: e.g. `$derived($page.props.flash?.error ?? null)` and a block with destructive styling (`bg-destructive/10 text-destructive`). Example: Exam Session Show shows both success and error messages in context.

